' ============================================================================
' EdgeIteration_scripts__S1ScriptsOnlyDeployPhase0.puml
'
' Purpose : PlantUML sequence diagram for scenario S1 of the @NikolaiGogol /
'           _scripts edge-iteration workflow on @terra.
' RFC     : docs/rfc/RFC-0001-edge-iteration-workflow.md
' Scenarios: docs/rfc/RFC-0001-edge-iteration-scenarios.md (authoritative
'           analyst catalogue; this file renders the scenario below).
' Date    : 2026-10-29
' Base    : 004ee9e
'
' Split from the former single-file EdgeIteration_scripts.puml so each diagram renders to its
' own file. Render with: plantuml -tpng -tsvg docs/_diagrams/*.puml
'
' Shared facts:
'   source    = $HOME/.bookmarks/shared-projects/ChronoIndex/2026/ConvPlatProv-HomeServer__HomeAssistant/@NikolaiGogol
'   target    = /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts
'   container = HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol
'
' Phase 0 = deploy scripts as-is.
'   /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts is a DEBUG SURFACE:
'   no bind mount, no compose change, tags [scripts, debug], and it is not
'   implied by `container`. It is not the deployment path.
'
' Style: one start/end block per scenario, autonumber per diagram,
'        participants declared only where used (cf. docs/Deploy#NixContainer.puml).
' ============================================================================

@startuml
autonumber
title S1 — Scripts-only deploy (Phase 0)

actor Operator
participant "Control node" as ControlNode
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir

Operator -> ControlNode : run TAGS=scripts via Makefile.NixosScripts
ControlNode -> Ansible : ansible-playbook -i hosts.ini deploy-nikolaigogol.yml --tags scripts
Ansible -> ControlNode : assert source dir, switch-nixos.sh and Makefile exist
alt source assertion fails
    Ansible --> Operator : fail with the expected upstream path and remediation
else source complete
    Ansible -> Terra : ensure _scripts exists with mode 0755
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : read .deploy-state when present
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash target tree excluding .env and .deploy-state*
    ScriptsDir --> Ansible : current tree_sha256
    alt clean (no manifest or tree_sha256 matches)
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync --checksum --omit-dir-times with delete=false
        note right of Ansible
          Excludes: .git, .env, result-*,
          node_modules, .yarn/cache
        end note
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : render .env with mode 0600
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash deployed tree and write .deploy-state when absent or changed
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : bash -n each *.sh
        Ansible -> Terra : docker compose -f docker-compose-system.yml config -q
        Ansible -> Terra : make -n image-name
        Terra --> Ansible : verification exit 0
        Ansible --> Operator : report scripts path, changed state and verification
    else drift (hash differs and force=false)
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : sha256sum -c .deploy-state.drift
        Ansible --> Operator : fail and list the drifted paths
        Operator -> Ansible : re-run with -e nikolaigogol_scripts_force=true
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync overwrite, render .env, rewrite manifest
        Ansible --> Operator : report forced deploy
    end
end
note over ScriptsDir
  delete=false leaves stale files and debugger additions in place.
  The manifest and drift report are the visibility mechanism.
  Missing docker or make skips only that validation probe; the role continues.
end note
@enduml
